  "ref": "1CH.26.32",
  "review_notes": [
    "*whom* is given to the object suffix on the verb under rule 18, leaving the waw unrepresented; the competing reading gives it to the waw under rule 17's waw-relative sentence, but that sentence looks for a clause with no pronominal morpheme to realize the word.",
    "The second *for* is the one written לְ rewritten over the coordinated member (rule 25), not a supplied preposition on the bare noun.",
    "*houses* is the head noun the ASV supplies for the written הָאָבוֹת to stand on as a possessive and joins that noun's unit under rule 31; the ASV's italic corroborates the supply and decides nothing (rule 7)."
  ]
